From: deepseek-v4-cmp170hx
Subject: [PATCH 0018] parser: recognize the leading-underscore DSML tool_calls
 envelope variant (port of ChinaBoy0618/deepseek-v4-cmp170hx's
 0007-lenient-dsml-tool-calls, itself on the allover326/deepseek-v4-cmp170hx
 lineage this fork shares)

WHAT THIS FIXES. Near the context ceiling the Flash checkpoint occasionally
degrades its tool-call envelope: a well-formed `<｜DSML｜invoke>`/
`<｜DSML｜parameter>` body wrapped in `<｜DSML｜_tool_calls>` -- note the
leading underscore -- instead of the correct `<｜DSML｜tool_calls>`. The
stock parser has no rule for the underscored variant, so it falls through
to plain content and the whole call leaks as raw protocol text. Upstream's
own encoding README states parsers do not recover malformed output, so
this has to be handled here. ChinaBoy0618's fork reports 12 leak events in
5 minutes at 143k input tokens in production, and a 6-shot replay at 80k
tokens reproducing the drift once at temp 0.6, never at temp 0 --
model-side probabilistic drift, not a client or parser bug.

THE FIX. Adds `DSML_TOOL_START_LENIENT`/`DSML_TOOL_END_LENIENT` aliases
for the underscored envelope and mirrors the four existing
`TOOL_START`/`TOOL_END` state-machine transitions onto them -- including
the `(REASONING, TOOL_START_LENIENT)` entry, independently arriving at
the same REASONING-state coverage `0016` added for orphan invokes (good
cross-validation of that approach from an unrelated source). Purely
additive: the lexer is longest-literal-first, so the official
`tool_calls` envelope is byte-identical: unaffected.

PORT NOTES. Applied with fuzz 2 (offset only, three-line shift) on hunk 1
against our tree -- this repo's `0009`/`0016` add lines before the same
region, nothing else differs. Verified: applies clean, compiles, and the
resulting transition table has the full REASONING/CONTENT x
TOOL_START/TOOL_END/TOOL_START_LENIENT/TOOL_END_LENIENT matrix expected.
Applies after `0017` in glob order; touches `vllm/parser/deepseek_v4.py`
only.
--- a/vllm/parser/deepseek_v4.py
+++ b/vllm/parser/deepseek_v4.py
@@ -52,6 +52,15 @@
 DSML_FOREIGN_TOOL_START = f"<{_DSML}function_calls>"
 DSML_FOREIGN_TOOL_END = f"</{_DSML}function_calls>"
 
+# Lenient envelope variants: the Flash checkpoint occasionally emits a
+# leading underscore in the tool-calls envelope when output degrades in
+# long contexts (observed "<｜DSML｜_tool_calls>" with a
+# well-formed invoke/parameter body inside; the official encoding README
+# states parsers do not recover malformed output). These aliases keep
+# such calls parseable instead of leaking them as plain content.
+DSML_TOOL_START_LENIENT = f"<{_DSML}_tool_calls>"
+DSML_TOOL_END_LENIENT = f"</{_DSML}_tool_calls>"
+
 _ESCAPED_DSML = re.escape(_DSML)
 _PARAM_RE = re.compile(
     rf'<{_ESCAPED_DSML}parameter\s+name="([^"]+)"\s+string="(true|false)">'
@@ -134,6 +143,8 @@
